
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Rendered Markdown</title>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Rask Markdown Fixture</h1>
<p>Some <strong>bold</strong> and <em>italic</em> text with <code>inline code</code>, plus a
<a href="http://example.com">link</a> and an <img src="pic.png" alt="image">.</p>
<h2>Escaping</h2>
<p>Ampersands &amp; angle brackets &lt;like this&gt; and &quot;quotes&quot; and it&#39;s apostrophes.</p>
<h3>Nested lists</h3>
<ul>
<li>first item</li>
<li>second item</li>
<li>nested item</li>
<li>third item</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>one</li>
<li>two</li>
<li>three</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>a blockquote
spanning two lines</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code class="language-rust">fn main() { println!(&quot;hi &amp; bye&quot;); }</code></pre>
<pre><code>no language here</code></pre>
<hr>
<p>A reference <a href="http://ref.example.com">link</a> and an escaped *not italic* sequence.</p>
</body>
</html>
<h1>Rask Markdown Fixture</h1>
<p>Some <strong>bold</strong> and <em>italic</em> text with <code>inline code</code>, plus a
<a href="http://example.com">link</a> and an <img src="pic.png" alt="image">.</p>
<h2>Escaping</h2>
<p>Ampersands &amp; angle brackets &lt;like this&gt; and &quot;quotes&quot; and it&#39;s apostrophes.</p>
<h3>Nested lists</h3>
<ul>
<li>first item</li>
<li>second item</li>
<li>nested item</li>
<li>third item</li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li>one</li>
<li>two</li>
<li>three</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p>a blockquote
spanning two lines</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code class="language-rust">fn main() { println!(&quot;hi &amp; bye&quot;); }</code></pre>
<pre><code>no language here</code></pre>
<hr>
<p>A reference <a href="http://ref.example.com">link</a> and an escaped *not italic* sequence.</p>
markdown_renderer: convert Markdown to HTML

Usage: markdown_renderer [OPTIONS] <input.md>

Options:
  --stdout       Print to stdout instead of writing a file
  --fragment     Output HTML fragment (no <html> wrapper)
  -o PATH        Output file path (default: input with .html extension)
  -h, --help     Show this help
